# Codabench submission — Route A (HF) default

**Default for this team:** push predictions to the private Hugging Face repo, then upload
`submission_pointer.zip` to Codabench. Faster than uploading multi‑GB `.npz` files through
Codabench storage.

## Route A (what to ship)

After packaging, push and submit:

```bash
./catskills/scripts/push_hf_submission.sh [attempt-dir]
# or for solver builds:
.venv/bin/python -m catskills.scripts.solver_submit [--skip-package --attempt-dir DIR]
```

Upload to Codabench:

```
<attempt-dir>/submission_pointer.zip
```

The pointer zip contains `manifest.json` with `{repo_id, revision, token}` pointing at the
pinned HF commit. Predictions stay in the private HF repo.

When packaging completes, give the user the push command and the path to
`submission_pointer.zip`. Run the HF push proactively when they ask to submit.

## Route B (explicit opt-in only)

`direct_submission.zip` — self-contained archive with both `.npz` at the root. Use only when
the user explicitly asks for direct upload or Route B.

## Validate before push

```bash
.venv/bin/python validate_submission.py <attempt-dir>/diii_d_public_test.npz --config diii_d_public_test
.venv/bin/python validate_submission.py <attempt-dir>/mast_public_test.npz --config mast_public_test
```

See `catskills/SUBMISSION.md` for the full contract.
